* eda_boost - behavioural fixed-output boost regulator (part of ai-eda, see LICENSE)
*
* Pins: vin gnd vout shdn
* The output is `vset` behind `rout`, but it can only source current (a boost converter
* cannot pull its output down). The input draws the output power divided by `eta`
* (percent) plus the quiescent current `iq` while running. The regulator starts once VIN
* rises above `von` and keeps running down to `voff` (modelled as one threshold between
* them); SHDN, pulled up to VIN through 100 kohm, turns it off below about 0.4 V.
* Not modelled: ripple, the switch current limit, soft start.
*
.subckt eda_boost vin gnd vout shdn
+ params: vset=5 eta=85 iq=0.5m von=0.5 voff=0.3 rout=0.05
.param vth = {(von + voff) / 2}
Rpu vin shdn 100k
* Enable: 1 while VIN is above the threshold and SHDN is high.
Ben en gnd V = 0.5 * (1 + tanh((v(vin, gnd) - {vth}) / 0.02))
+ * 0.5 * (1 + tanh((v(shdn, gnd) - 0.6) / 0.05))
Ren en gnd 1Meg
* Output: a current source that drives VOUT towards vset (never sinks).
Bout gnd vout I = max({vset} * v(en, gnd) - v(vout, gnd), 0) / {rout}
Rleak vout gnd 10Meg
* Input: power balance plus quiescent current.
Bin vin gnd I = v(vout, gnd) * max({vset} * v(en, gnd) - v(vout, gnd), 0) / {rout}
+ / ({eta} / 100 * max(v(vin, gnd), {voff})) + {iq} * v(en, gnd)
.ends eda_boost
